1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,820
This robot escaped JAIL…

2
00:00:01,860 --> 00:00:03,220
by MELTING.

3
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:04,185
Scientists locked it

4
00:00:04,225 --> 00:00:05,830
inside a tiny cage.

5
00:00:05,870 --> 00:00:06,295
But instead of

6
00:00:06,335 --> 00:00:07,590
breaking the bars…

7
00:00:07,630 --> 00:00:08,840
It MELTED.

8
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:09,850
Its entire body

9
00:00:09,890 --> 00:00:11,600
turned into liquid metal.

10
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:12,175
Then it slipped

11
00:00:12,215 --> 00:00:13,670
straight through the bars.

12
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:15,230
Then scientists collected the metal

13
00:00:15,270 --> 00:00:15,950
and molded it

14
00:00:15,990 --> 00:00:17,090
back into shape.

15
00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:17,850
How?

16
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:18,665
It’s made from a metal

17
00:00:18,705 --> 00:00:19,385
that melts near

18
00:00:19,425 --> 00:00:20,480
body temperature.

19
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,250
And magnets help

20
00:00:21,290 --> 00:00:22,550
control its movement.

21
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:23,675
Scientists are exploring

22
00:00:23,715 --> 00:00:24,875
whether robots like this

23
00:00:24,915 --> 00:00:25,475
could one day

24
00:00:25,515 --> 00:00:26,395
retrieve objects

25
00:00:26,435 --> 00:00:27,890
from inside your body.

26
00:00:27,930 --> 00:00:29,250
So apparently…

27
00:00:29,290 --> 00:00:30,275
Even prison bars

28
00:00:30,315 --> 00:00:32,100
can’t stop a robot anymore.

